note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR GPL-2.0-only
note boot: the GB20B GSP start-up (12 register steps) as a step machine. Omega decides every register
note access; the kernel glue only performs the one action it is handed and calls again.
note The chip in the DGX Spark reports PMC_BOOT_42 0x1bba1000: architecture 0x1b, implementation 0xb,
note which NVIDIA's driver dispatches as GB20B (open-gpu-kernel-modules 580.173.02, MIT,
note generated/g_kernel_sec2_nvoc.c:674-953). Steps 0 and 6 are the GB20B HALs; the rest is shared with
note GB10B. The C reference of this unit is tests/host/gb20b_mmio.c (same register order, checked on
note tests/host/gb20b_sim.c by tests/host/parity_boot.c). Sources per step:
note 0 wait FWSEC done: PMC scratch 0x5e0 == 0xff (ksec2WaitForSecureBoot_GB20B, kernel_sec2_gb20b.c:541-575),
note 1 wait SEC2 EMEM channel 0 empty (QUEUE_HEAD == QUEUE_TAIL), 2-4 write the packet through EMEMC/EMEMD
note with auto-increment and check the write pointer, 5 QUEUE_TAIL then QUEUE_HEAD (doorbell)
note (ksec2SendPacket_GB10B, the HAL GB20B also takes, g_kernel_sec2_nvoc.c:802-804),
note 6 wait for the SEC2 reply (MSGQ_HEAD != MSGQ_TAIL), read it through EMEMC/EMEMD with read
note auto-increment, acknowledge it (MSGQ_TAIL = head, then MSGQ_HEAD = head) and check it: one MCTP
note packet, vendor-defined PCI message 0x7e, vendor 0x10de, NVDM type SEC2_RESPONSE 0x15 or SMBPBI 0x18,
note error code 0 (ksec2SendBootCommands_GB20B :1034, ksec2SendAndReadMessage_IMPL kernel_sec2.c:496-523,
note ksec2ReadPacket_GB20B :481-537, ksec2GetPacketInfo_GB20B :235-281, ksec2ProcessCommandResponse_GB20B
note :385-418). GB10B instead polls SEC2 MAILBOX0 for 0xc001cafe; GB20B never reads that register.
note 7 wait GSP HWCFG2 mask released, 8 wait lockdown released or an
note FMC code, 9 GSP MAILBOX0 must be 0, 10 FALCON_OS = appVersion, 11 RISC-V CPUCTL ACTIVE (bit 7).
note
note st (32 ulong, caller zeroes it and sets the inputs):
note   0 pc (0 = start)  1 packet bytes 1..1024  2 FMC boot-argument address  3 appVersion
note   4..7 poll budgets: 4 steps 0 and 1, 5 step 6, 6 step 7, 7 step 8   8 poll counter
note   9 packet byte index, then reply dword index   10 EMEM start, then EMEMC after the reply read
note   11 SEC2 QUEUE_HEAD read in step 1, then MSGQ_HEAD
note   12 stage: 0 ok, 1 arg, 2 busy, 3 emem, 4 sec2 (no reply), 5 mask, 6 lockdown, 7 fmc, 8 riscv,
note      9 secure boot not done, 10 reply refused (31 says why), 11 SEC2 reported an error (19)
note   13..16 polls used by steps 1, 6, 7, 8   17 dwords   18 EMEMC after the packet write
note   19 reply error code   20 reply bytes   21 HWCFG2   22 GSP MAILBOX0   23 GSP MAILBOX1   24 CPUCTL
note   25 polls used by step 0   26 reply command type   27 PMC scratch as last read
note   28 reply dword 0 (MCTP)   29 reply dword 1 (message header)   30 reply task id
note   31 reply refusal: 1 size, 2 read pointer, 3 not one packet, 4 message type, 5 vendor,
note      6 NVDM type, 7 too short
note act (4 ulong) written on result 0: 0 kind (1 read, 2 write, 3 pause between polls), 1 BAR0 offset,
note   2 value to write. obs = the value the previous read returned (0 after a write or a pause).
note Result: 0 = do act and call again, 1 = finished (st 12 holds the stage).
note Register offsets in decimal (aien-calc receipts in docs/STATUS.md):
note PMC SCRATCH_RESET_PLUS_2 0x5e0 = 1504; SEC2 EMEMC0 0x840ac0 = 8653504, EMEMD0 0x840ac4 = 8653508,
note QHEAD0 0x840c00 = 8653824, QTAIL0 0x840c04 = 8653828, MSGQ_HEAD0 0x840c80 = 8653952,
note MSGQ_TAIL0 0x840c84 = 8653956; GSP MAILBOX0 0x110040, MAILBOX1 0x110044, FALCON_OS 0x110080,
note HWCFG2 0x1100f4, RISC-V CPUCTL 0x111388. EMEMC bit 24 0x1000000 = 16777216 write auto-increment,
note bit 25 0x2000000 = 33554432 read auto-increment; locked 0xbadf4100 under mask 0xffffff00,
note lockdown bit 13, active bit 7. omc befb8199 refuses `const` in function mode
note (error 9 at end of input), so these appear below as decimal literals.
fn bact act edit ulong 4 kind ulong off ulong val ulong to ulong
put act 0 kind
put act 1 off
put act 2 val
ret 0
end
fn bfin st edit ulong 32 stage ulong to ulong
put st 12 stage
put st 0 99
ret 1
end
note EMEMC: block 15:8 times 64 dwords plus offset 7:2 (gsp_mmio.c emem_dwords).
fn ememdw v ulong to ulong
ret add mul and shr v 8 255 64 and shr v 2 63
end
note Little-endian dword of packet bytes i..i+3, zero beyond the packet length n.
fn pword pkt view uchar 1024 i ulong n ulong to ulong
w = ulong 0
for k ulong 4
if lt add i k n
w = or w shl ulong get pkt add i k mul k 8
end
end
ret w
end
note Step 0: FWSEC finished the secure boot: PMC scratch 0x5e0 reads exactly 0xff. pc 1 read, 2 decide.
fn bstep0 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 1
put st 0 2
ret bact act 1 1504 0
end
put st 27 obs
n = get st 8
if eq obs 255
put st 25 n
put st 8 0
put st 0 10
ret 2
end
if ge n get st 4
put st 25 n
ret bfin st 9
end
put st 8 add n 1
put st 0 1
ret bact act 3 0 0
end
note Step 1: SEC2 channel empty. pc 10 read HEAD, 11 read TAIL, 12 compare.
fn bstep1 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 10
put st 0 11
ret bact act 1 8653824 0
end
if eq pc 11
put st 11 obs
put st 0 12
ret bact act 1 8653828 0
end
n = get st 8
if eq get st 11 obs
put st 13 n
put st 8 0
put st 0 20
ret 2
end
if ge n get st 4
put st 13 n
ret bfin st 2
end
put st 8 add n 1
put st 0 10
ret bact act 3 0 0
end
note Steps 2-5: packet into EMEM, write pointer check, TAIL then HEAD.
fn bstep2 st edit ulong 32 pkt view uchar 1024 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 20
put st 0 21
ret bact act 2 8653504 16777216
end
if eq pc 21
put st 0 22
ret bact act 1 8653504 0
end
if eq pc 22
put st 10 ememdw obs
put st 9 0
put st 0 23
end
pc = get st 0
n = get st 1
i = get st 9
if eq pc 23
if lt i n
put st 9 add i 4
ret bact act 2 8653508 pword pkt i n
end
put st 0 25
ret bact act 1 8653504 0
end
if eq pc 25
dw = div add n 3 4
put st 17 dw
put st 18 obs
if ne sub ememdw obs get st 10 dw
ret bfin st 3
end
put st 0 26
ret bact act 2 8653828 sub mul dw 4 4
end
put st 8 0
put st 0 30
ret bact act 2 8653824 0
end
note Step 6: SEC2 replied: MSGQ_HEAD != MSGQ_TAIL. pc 30 read HEAD, 31 read TAIL, 32 compare.
fn bstep6 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 30
put st 0 31
ret bact act 1 8653952 0
end
if eq pc 31
put st 11 obs
put st 0 32
ret bact act 1 8653956 0
end
n = get st 8
if ne get st 11 obs
put st 14 n
put st 8 0
put st 0 70
ret 2
end
if ge n get st 5
put st 14 n
ret bfin st 4
end
put st 8 add n 1
put st 0 30
ret bact act 3 0 0
end
note Step 6, the check after the acknowledgement, in the driver's order: read pointer, packet state
note with the header checks of a first packet, one packet only, NVDM type, length, error code.
note The `lt sz 8` check is the driver's (kernel_sec2_gb20b.c:329-333) and is never taken here: under
note 8 bytes only dword 0 was read, st 29 is 0 and the message-type check has already refused.
fn brspchk st edit ulong 32 to ulong
sz = get st 20
if ne ememdw get st 10 div sz 4
put st 31 2
ret bfin st 10
end
d0 = get st 28
d1 = get st 29
som = and shr d0 31 1
eom = and shr d0 30 1
if eq som 1
if ne and d1 127 126
put st 31 4
ret bfin st 10
end
if ne and shr d1 8 65535 4318
put st 31 5
ret bfin st 10
end
if lt sz 8
put st 31 7
ret bfin st 10
end
end
if or ne som 1 ne eom 1
put st 31 3
ret bfin st 10
end
t = and shr d1 24 255
if and ne t 21 ne t 24
put st 31 6
ret bfin st 10
end
if lt sz 20
put st 31 7
ret bfin st 10
end
if ne get st 19 0
ret bfin st 11
end
put st 8 0
put st 0 40
ret 2
end
note Step 6, the reply itself. pc 70 read HEAD, 71 read TAIL, 72 size and EMEMC, 73/74 the dwords,
note 75 EMEMC back, 76 TAIL = head, 77 HEAD = head, then the check. Tail points at the last dword.
fn brsp st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 70
put st 0 71
ret bact act 1 8653952 0
end
if eq pc 71
put st 11 obs
put st 0 72
ret bact act 1 8653956 0
end
if eq pc 72
sz = and sub add add obs 4294967296 4 get st 11 4294967295
put st 20 sz
if or lt sz 4 gt sz 1024
put st 31 1
ret bfin st 10
end
put st 9 0
put st 0 73
ret bact act 2 8653504 33554432
end
if eq pc 74
i = get st 9
if lt i 3
put st add 28 i obs
end
if eq i 3
put st 26 obs
end
if eq i 4
put st 19 obs
end
put st 9 add i 1
put st 0 73
end
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 73
if lt get st 9 div get st 20 4
put st 0 74
ret bact act 1 8653508 0
end
put st 0 75
ret bact act 1 8653504 0
end
if eq pc 75
put st 10 obs
put st 0 76
ret bact act 2 8653956 get st 11
end
if eq pc 76
put st 0 77
ret bact act 2 8653952 get st 11
end
ret brspchk st
end
note Step 7: GSP target mask released: HWCFG2 non-zero and not 0xbadf41xx.
fn bstep7 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 40
put st 0 41
ret bact act 1 1114356 0
end
put st 21 obs
n = get st 8
if and ne obs 0 ne and obs 4294967040 3135193344
put st 15 n
put st 8 0
put st 0 50
ret 2
end
if ge n get st 6
put st 15 n
ret bfin st 5
end
put st 8 add n 1
put st 0 40
ret bact act 3 0 0
end
note Step 8 continued: not released yet; budget check, then pause or give up.
fn bwait8 st edit ulong 32 act edit ulong 4 to ulong
n = get st 8
if ge n get st 7
put st 16 n
put st 0 56
ret bact act 1 1114180 0
end
put st 8 add n 1
put st 0 50
ret bact act 3 0 0
end
note Step 8: lockdown released or an FMC code. MAILBOX0:MAILBOX1 equal to the FMC argument address
note means not read yet (keep waiting, HWCFG2 not read on that pass, as the driver).
fn bstep8 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
pa = get st 2
if eq pc 50
put st 0 51
ret bact act 1 1114176 0
end
if eq pc 56
put st 23 obs
ret bfin st 6
end
if eq pc 51
put st 22 obs
if and ne obs 0 eq obs and pa 4294967295
put st 0 52
ret bact act 1 1114180 0
end
put st 0 53
ret bact act 1 1114356 0
end
if eq pc 52
put st 23 obs
if eq obs shr pa 32
ret bwait8 st act
end
put st 0 53
ret bact act 1 1114356 0
end
put st 21 obs
if or eq and obs 8192 0 ne get st 22 0
put st 16 get st 8
put st 0 60
ret bact act 1 1114176 0
end
ret bwait8 st act
end
note Steps 9-11: FMC error check, FALCON_OS, RISC-V active.
fn bstep9 st edit ulong 32 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 60
put st 22 obs
if ne obs 0
ret bfin st 7
end
put st 0 62
ret bact act 2 1114240 and get st 3 4294967295
end
if eq pc 62
put st 0 63
ret bact act 1 1119112 0
end
put st 24 obs
if eq and obs 128 0
ret bfin st 8
end
ret bfin st 0
end
note Entry. Each call runs at most a few internal transitions (helpers return 2) before an action.
fn agpu_boot_next st edit ulong 32 pkt view uchar 1024 obs ulong act edit ulong 4 to ulong
if eq get st 0 0
for k ulong 24
put st add k 8 0
end
n = get st 1
if or eq n 0 gt n 1024
ret bfin st 1
end
put st 0 1
end
r = ulong 2
while eq r 2 bound 8
pc = get st 0
if eq pc 99
ret 1
end
if lt pc 10
r = bstep0 st obs act
else
if lt pc 20
r = bstep1 st obs act
else
if lt pc 30
r = bstep2 st pkt obs act
else
if lt pc 40
r = bstep6 st obs act
else
if lt pc 50
r = bstep7 st obs act
else
if lt pc 60
r = bstep8 st obs act
else
if lt pc 70
r = bstep9 st obs act
else
r = brsp st obs act
end
end
end
end
end
end
end
end
ret r
end
